{
  "id": "kth-largest-element-in-an-array",
  "title": "Kth Largest Element in an Array",
  "difficulty": "medium",
  "categories": ["heap", "sorting"],
  "descriptionMd": "Given an integer array `nums` and an integer `k`, return the value that would sit in position `k` if the array were sorted from largest to smallest.\n\nDuplicates count separately: in `[5, 5, 1]` the 1st and 2nd largest are both `5`.\n\n**Example 1**\n\n```\nnums = [3, 2, 1, 5, 6, 4], k = 2\n→ 5\n```\n\n**Example 2**\n\n```\nnums = [3, 2, 3, 1, 2, 4, 5, 5, 6], k = 4\n→ 4\n```\nIn descending order the array reads 6, 5, 5, 4, … so the 4th value is 4.\n\n**Follow-up:** sorting works in O(n log n). Can you avoid sorting the whole array?",
  "constraints": ["1 ≤ k ≤ nums.length ≤ 10⁵", "-10⁴ ≤ nums[i] ≤ 10⁴"],
  "hints": ["You only care about the k biggest values — the rest can be thrown away as you go.", "Keep a collection of the k largest seen so far. Which of them do you need to check against each new number?"],
  "signature": {
    "functionName": "findKthLargest",
    "params": [{ "name": "nums", "type": "int[]" }, { "name": "k", "type": "int" }],
    "returns": "int"
  },
  "comparator": "exact",
  "tests": [
